.env

# iCloud conflict copies ("index 2.html", "app 3.js"). This project lives under a synced
# Documents folder, and a build that rewrites src/main/resources/static/ regularly produces
# them. Committing one would ship a duplicate asset inside the jar; a stale copy in target/
# also breaks Spring Boot's main-class detection, since it sees two candidates.
